<section class="wrap band">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">What to do now</p><h2>Four moves, in order.</h2></div>
    <div class="steps"><div><p class="n">01</p><h4>Identify affected clients</h4><p>Developers, promoters, strategic land funds. Every in-scope agreement completed since 8 June 2026 needs collating now, ready for the service opening.</p></div><div><p class="n">02</p><h4>Design the intake</h4><p>Agreement type, parties with company numbers, titles, dates, duration, extensions, exercise conditions, land affected. Capture it at completion, not six months later.</p></div><div><p class="n">03</p><h4>Sort the spatial data</h4><p>Where a right affects part of a title HMLR wants a machine-readable file on British National Grid. Get it from the surveyor at contract stage. Scanned PDFs are refused.</p></div><div><p class="n">04</p><h4>Confirm the regulated submitter</h4><p>Decide which named individuals will file, and how their authorisation is evidenced. HMLR has said unregulated staff cannot submit even under supervision.</p></div></div>
