<section class="wrap band">
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="body"><h3>Why this departs from normal HMLR practice</h3>
<p>Most Land Registry applications can be lodged by a wide cohort of staff inside a conveyancing firm. The contractual control service is restricted to individually regulated conveyancers acting in their own capacity. Firms that rely on paralegal-heavy registration teams need a different workflow for these submissions.</p>
<h3>What HMLR has said about the service</h3>
<p>HM Land Registry is developing the service with conveyancers and has run user research since mid-2026. Feedback about the number of steps led them to combine related contract details into a single workflow. HMLR will also provide online mapping tools so a conveyancer can identify affected land without uploading a spatial file where that is simpler. A further practice guide with technical detail is promised; it has not been published yet.</p>
<h3>Data you will need per right</h3>
<ul>
<li>Type of right: option, conditional contract, pre-emption, or qualifying promotion right.</li>
<li>Grantor and grantee, with company registration numbers where companies. Individuals may need date and place of birth for identification.</li>
<li>Registered title numbers affected, and whether the whole or part.</li>
<li>Date of grant, control period, extension provisions, and the conditions on which the right can be exercised.</li>
<li>Spatial extent, as GeoJSON or Shapefile on British National Grid, where only part of a title is affected.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Deadlines you now own on the client’s behalf</h3>
<p>Rights granted 8 June 2026 to 5 April 2027: submit by 6 October 2027. Rights granted, assigned, varied or exercised on or after 6 April 2027: 60 calendar days from the event. Build both into your matter management, because the consequence of missing one is HMLR refusing the notice or restriction that protects your client’s right.</p>
<h3>Fee opportunity</h3>
<p>Each reportable event is chargeable work. A firm with a clear intake, a named regulated submitter and a spatial-data process will win the developer clients who have 40 options to file by October 2027 and no idea where their plans are.</p></div>
